## Disclosed limitations, please adjudicate

1. **The mirror is inert** — populated by fetch, pruned by fetch, read by
   nothing. The payoff is independent of readability (prune safe by construction,
   a fetch refspec able to exist at all, structural provenance). Divergence
   reporting is etude-eje; it depends on which-remote provenance, so etude-cng
   must land before or with it.
2. **Mirror refs pin objects.** A plain `git fetch` now downloads the remote's
   etude object graph and mirror refs keep it reachable, so `git gc` will not
   reclaim it. No expiry exists until etude-26i, including after a remote is
   renamed or removed. Documented in `docs/init.md` with a hand-cleanup command.
3. **Not injective for slash-containing remote names** (etude-cng), bounded to
   mirror-only aliasing as described above.
4. **`refs/etude/` now means "everything here gets pushed"**, a consequence of
   leaving the push refspec broad. Documented, so a future local-only ref is not
   placed there.
